# API Route Standards

> Full production checklist: `docs/PRODUCTION_STANDARDS.md` §3. This file is the quick reference for route handlers.

## Shared helpers (`@/lib/api-route`)
- `requireApiSession()` — auth + typed session; use `isApiError()` to branch.
- `parseJsonBody(req)`, `parsePagination(searchParams)`, `paginationMeta(total, page, limit)`.
- `apiOk`, `apiCreated`, `apiList`, `apiInvalidInput`, `apiNotFound`, `apiPlanLimit`, `apiConflict`.
- `handleApiRoute(async () => …)` — wraps handler; maps Prisma P2002 → 409.

## Authentication
- Prefer `requireApiSession()` over raw `auth()` in new/refactored routes.
- Return 401 if not authenticated.
- For admin routes, verify `session.user.role === "ADMIN"`. Return 403 if not admin.

## Validation
- Parse body safely: `const body = await req.json().catch(() => null)` then Zod `safeParse`.
- Return consistent JSON: `{ data: T }` for success; errors per `docs/PRODUCTION_STANDARDS.md` §3.3.
- Validation failures: 400 with `{ error: "Invalid input", details: parsed.error.flatten() }` when useful.

## HTTP Status Codes
- 200: OK
- 201: Created
- 400: Bad Request (validation error)
- 401: Unauthorized
- 402: Plan limit / upgrade required (use for quotas — not 403)
- 403: Admin-only forbidden (role check)
- 404: Not found **or** resource owned by another user (do not use 403 for IDOR)
- 409: Conflict (duplicate unique constraint)
- 500: Server Error

## Pagination (required on new list GETs)
- Query: `?page=1&limit=20` (default 20, max 100)
- Return: `{ data: T[], pagination: { page, limit, total, totalPages } }`
- Use minimal `select` — list endpoints must not return full nested graphs

## Cron Routes
- Verify `CRON_SECRET` header for all cron endpoints.
- Pattern: `if (req.headers.get("authorization") !== \`Bearer ${process.env.CRON_SECRET}\`) return 401`

## Plan Tier Limits
- Source of truth: `planLimits` in `@/lib/config` — use **`maxProjects`** (never `maxGoalsPerPlan` in new code).
- Count existing records before insert; reject over-limit with HTTP **402** + `{ error: "THING_LIMIT", message, upgradeUrl: "/pricing" }`.
- Reference: `src/app/api/areas/route.ts`, `src/app/api/notes/route.ts`.

## Idempotency
- Writes hitting `@@unique` must use `upsert` or catch Prisma P2002 → 409 — never unhandled 500 on duplicate submit.

## PARA Naming
- Use the new model names in code: `db.project`, `db.task`, `db.system`, `db.projectCheckIn`, `db.projectCheckpoint`, `db.area`, `db.vision`, `db.note`, `db.resource`, `db.drift`, `db.dailyState`.
- URL paths still use legacy segments where the dynamic param exists (`[goalId]`); destructure into a new local name: `const { goalId: projectId } = await params`.

## Pattern Example
```ts
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth"
import { db } from "@/lib/db"
import { planLimits } from "@/lib/config"
import { NextResponse } from "next/server"
import { z } from "zod"

const schema = z.object({ title: z.string().min(1), areaId: z.string().optional() })

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const session = await auth()
  if (!session?.user) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 })
  }
  const body = await req.json()
  const parsed = schema.safeParse(body)
  if (!parsed.success) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "Invalid input" }, { status: 400 })
  }

  const plan = await db.yearlyPlan.findFirst({
    where: { userId: session.user.id, status: "ACTIVE" },
    select: { id: true, _count: { select: { projects: true } } },
  })
  if (!plan) return NextResponse.json({ error: "No active plan" }, { status: 404 })

  const tier = (session.user.planTier ?? "FREE") as keyof typeof planLimits
  if (plan._count.projects >= planLimits[tier].maxProjects) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: "Project limit reached", upgradeUrl: "/pricing" },
      { status: 402 }
    )
  }

  const project = await db.project.create({
    data: { ...parsed.data, planId: plan.id },
  })
  return NextResponse.json({ data: project }, { status: 201 })
}
```
